        "## Krea 2 Turbo: text-to-image, Hires. fix\n\n[Krea 2](https://huggingface.co/krea/Krea-2-Turbo) (Krea, Qwen3-VL 4B text encoder, Qwen-Image VAE) is an aesthetic\ntext-to-image model. **Turbo** is the 8-step TDM-distilled variant; **Raw** (`krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors`) is the undistilled base, see the\nRaw workflow.\n\n**Settings**: 8 steps, CFG 1, euler, simple, 1024×1024 (up to 2048×2048). The negative conditioning is zeroed: at CFG 1\na negative prompt has no effect, so the Generate tab shows none. **CFG above 1 degrades the image.**\n\n**Prompts**: full descriptive sentences (subject, setting, composition, lighting, materials, mood), not tag\nlists. Stay well under ~500 tokens: very long prompts produce black images. `(word:1.2)` weights are not\nknown to work.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale, sampling method, schedule type; size (Width / Height) |\n| `ib:smp:1` | Hires. fix KSampler | Hires. fix: upscaler, scale, steps, denoising |\n| `ib:hr` | Hires. fix (If/Else Switch) | Hires. fix checkbox; Upscale button |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**Hires. fix**: Krea 2 renders up to 2048×2048 natively, so for a larger image prefer generating at the target size\n(composition changes with the size). Hires. fix keeps the composition: the upscaler model enlarges the first pass,\n**Resize to the hires size** brings it to the first pass size × *Upscale by* (1.5), and a second Turbo KSampler samples\nit at denoising 0.35 (8 steps at CFG 1; above about 0.5 it redraws details). Put any ESRGAN-type model into\n`models/upscale_models` ([RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Real-ESRGAN_repackaged/resolve/main/RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors) here); the loader must name an installed model even\nwhile Hires. fix is off. There is no official Krea guidance for a second pass.\n\n**Hires. fix ib:hr** (`If/Else Switch`) is the Hires. fix checkbox of the Generate tab: off, the first pass is saved\nand the Hires. fix nodes do not run. The **Upscale** button switches it on, generates the image again with its seed\nand parameters, and switches it back.\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt.\n\n**Style LoRAs** ([Comfy-Org/Krea-2/loras](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/tree/main/loras), strength 1.0) need\ntheir trigger words in the prompt, e.g. `<lora:krea2_darkbrush:1> monochrome ink wash style` (`darkbrush`: monochrome\nink wash style, `dotmatrix`: monochrome stippling style, `kidsdrawing`: naive expressive sketch style, `neondrip`:\ntextured abstract style, `rainywindow`: rainy window style, `retroanime`: purple retro anime style, `softwatercolor`:\nart deco watercolor style, `sunsetblur`: ethereal motion blur style, `vintagetarot`: vintage tarot style).\n\nThe Generate tab has no References panel and the ControlNet tab no units: the stock nodes take no reference images\nfor Krea 2 (the Identity Edit and Style Reference LoRAs need their own node packs), and its control LoRAs are not\nControlNets.\n\n## Model Links\n\n[Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2) also has `*_bf16` and `*_int8_convrot` diffusion models of\nRaw and Turbo, `krea2_turbo_mxfp8` / `krea2_turbo_nvfp4` (RTX 50), and the bf16 / int8 text encoders.\n\n**diffusion_models**: [krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors), [krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/diffusion_models/krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors) (one file for Raw and Turbo)\n**vae**: [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors) (the Qwen-Image VAE)\n**loras**: [krea2_darkbrush.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/loras/krea2_darkbrush.safetensors)\n\nKrea 2 is released under the Krea 2 Community License.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: Krea 2 Turbo (Image Bench, all features)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
